❓Question
You are given an array nums containing 0, 1, and 2.
Sort the array in-place so that:
0 → 1 → 2
You cannot use the library's sorting function.

Example
Input: nums = [2,0,2,1,1,0]
Output: [0,0,1,1,2,2]

✅Approach — Dutch National Flag / Three Pointers
Use three pointers:
low   → position where next 0 should go
mid   → current element
high  → position where next 2 should go
There are three cases:
1. nums[mid] == 0
Swap nums[mid] with nums[low]
Move low++
Move mid++
2. nums[mid] == 1
1 is already in the correct middle area.
Just move mid++.
3. nums[mid] == 2
Swap nums[mid] with nums[high]
Move high--
Do not move mid, because the value coming from high still needs to be checked.

Code
class Solution {
    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        int low = 0;
        int mid = 0;
        int high = nums.length - 1;
        while (mid <= high) {
            if (nums[mid] == 0) {
                int temp = nums[low];
                nums[low] = nums[mid];
                nums[mid] = temp;
                mid++;
                low++;
            } else if (nums[mid] == 2) {
                int temp = nums[high];
                nums[high] = nums[mid];
                nums[mid] = temp;
                high--;
            } else {
                mid++;
            }
        }
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
